  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Men, Gender And AIDS: Focusing on men for transformation of behaviour and attitudes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#xb7; through educational workshops, it primarily seeks to contribute in the transformation of men&apos;s attitudes and behaviour in the context of HIV/AIDS.
&#xb7; through low scale research, it seeks to contribute to knowledge of what men really think, what they want and how they can contribute to a response to the AIDS epidemic.
&#xb7; through various networking processes, men and institutions will be mobilized to support this initiative.
&#xb7; through distribution of reading materials and information sessions in theological institutions and amongst clergy, to encourage the introduction of a focus on human rights for women, violence against women and children, and socialization into gender roles for women and men, into formation and training.
&#xb7; Through  information sessions amongst African traditional leaders, to raise awareness of gender issues, encouraging the examining attitudes, the perspectives of their beliefs and experiences, and providing resources so as to contribute to the change of behaviour and ultimately transforming society. 
&#xb7; The initiative focuses on the equal dignity of women and men, and seeks to expose and address areas where this has been distorted socially and theologically.</narrative>
  </description>
